{
  "title": "De dokter en de balie",
  "goal": "Use a small set of reflexive verbs and make clear, polite requests in service situations.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 1
      },
      "content": "De dokter en de balie",
      "id": "39d42fb6-2e31-4684-851d-a5f3488797fb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It is Tuesday 26 January 2027. In Dutch class at the central library, Marieke gives Sofia and Piotr two practice role-plays. They do not describe real appointments or problems. In examples, subjects are green, verbs blue, places purple, and the target forms are bold.",
      "id": "8b91c48c-a10d-4258-b2aa-edab440a963d"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Story: two role-plays",
      "id": "3c326a6d-e37b-4b32-99d5-db6a47587bab"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Marieke",
            "text": "We oefenen twee gesprekken. Eerst bij de huisarts, daarna bij de balie."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ik voel me niet lekker. Is dat goed Nederlands?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Marieke",
            "text": "Ja. Je zegt: Ik voel me niet lekker."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Piotr",
            "text": "En als ik zeg: Ik ben ziek?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Marieke",
            "text": "Dat kan ook. Dat is een andere zin."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Kunt u mij helpen? Ik wil een afspraak maken."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Marieke",
            "text": "Goed. En vraag rustig om herhaling als iets niet duidelijk is."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Piotr",
            "text": "Zou u dat kunnen herhalen, alstublieft?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Marieke",
            "text": "Prima. Dit is een oefening; we bellen niemand."
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "f1e16fc3-583b-4b7f-a34b-91f868203a44"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "de dokter",
              "meaning": "doctor",
              "forms": "de dokters",
              "id": "2b5ff7af-12fd-4b25-bd75-d0e7a7203bb9"
            },
            {
              "term": "het rollenspel",
              "meaning": "role-play",
              "forms": "de rollenspellen",
              "id": "21cbdb34-07f3-4e39-81f7-15ef906d6d50"
            },
            {
              "term": "zich voelen",
              "meaning": "to feel (oneself)",
              "forms": "voelt zich · voelde zich · zich gevoeld",
              "example": "Ik voel me niet lekker.",
              "id": "6dc1a373-4ed8-44a5-bc16-8c0329900d84"
            },
            {
              "term": "zich vergissen",
              "meaning": "to be mistaken",
              "forms": "vergist zich · vergiste zich · zich vergist",
              "example": "Ik vergis me soms.",
              "id": "be1ba753-4114-42c6-89de-c7a6e1628fed"
            },
            {
              "term": "de herhaling",
              "meaning": "repetition; repeating",
              "forms": "de herhalingen",
              "id": "86014e9a-fb94-4569-b685-482daf5c706e"
            },
            {
              "term": "ziek",
              "meaning": "ill",
              "id": "cc183a0f-e179-47b6-b70c-615e09a3780e"
            },
            {
              "term": "niet lekker",
              "meaning": "unwell; not feeling well",
              "example": "Ik voel me niet lekker.",
              "id": "2506d3c6-df39-476d-bea9-5550f285e10d"
            },
            {
              "term": "Ik voel me niet lekker.",
              "meaning": "I do not feel well.",
              "example": "Ik voel me niet lekker.",
              "note": "A common sentence for describing how you feel; it does not give a diagnosis.",
              "id": "3c5a92a6-8d10-42cc-adac-b214032be432"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "b9e6ac3f-85a7-41ca-9c88-1c121a6fcdce"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Reflexive pronouns",
      "id": "0006e477-2c06-4453-9853-b3187fa164b6"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Some Dutch verbs use a small pronoun that refers back to the subject. Learn the verb together with its pronoun. The set here is limited to four useful verbs.",
      "id": "b214b2dc-f7ed-4998-b0a7-8d59a3c2e03f"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "grammar",
        "icon": "book-open"
      },
      "content": "In a plain main clause, put the reflexive pronoun after the finite verb: Ik voel me. In an inverted clause, the subject comes first, then the finite verb, then the pronoun: Vandaag voel ik me beter.",
      "id": "9412ec8a-3b8c-4287-b14a-8288a1fa8009"
    },
    {
      "type": "columnList",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "props": {
                "level": 3
              },
              "content": "Subject + verb",
              "id": "01c01898-24c5-4534-9722-550ea6bf1eb3"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "ik voel me",
              "id": "cca3a815-1a17-4da2-9ca4-9f5f4f124909"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "jij wast je",
              "id": "cf3fb7ba-a4fe-42e6-8e54-7f1082dda3af"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "hij / zij vergist zich",
              "id": "33cd77c3-7675-40e5-bff1-33c6c4c4e77b"
            }
          ],
          "id": "ec2cb309-b4b6-48a7-a2d7-fab2d9603dd8"
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "props": {
                "level": 3
              },
              "content": "Plural",
              "id": "617a1581-6d6d-4df0-8230-cb29e5e02384"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "wij wassen ons",
              "id": "68b25c64-5059-42af-b711-9976b3ea2a87"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "jullie vergissen je",
              "id": "4d4c116e-91e1-4986-b4b1-907cd5a03a6b"
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "content": "zij voelen zich",
              "id": "a2605011-c088-4819-a16b-383f8fe67e59"
            }
          ],
          "id": "051c7222-9b04-4cfb-9da2-59ee0df0eb69"
        }
      ],
      "id": "d0ef3732-e93e-42b2-9ff4-65dde7614cab"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "I do not feel well.",
        "note": "Fixed situation language; this is not a diagnosis."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Ik voel me niet lekker.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "edae60c4-42d4-48e0-8b5e-0874aac6e949"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Today I feel better.",
        "note": "Fronted time expression: verb before subject."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Vandaag voel ik me beter.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "ec9abc5a-13f1-49e5-99da-b4b00547ef63"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "I wash myself at home.",
        "note": "The reflexive pronoun follows the finite verb."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Ik was me thuis.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "e34cbd19-a127-40a7-9019-8d9cf1e95791"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "We wash ourselves before eating.",
        "note": "Recycles time phrases."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Wij wassen ons voor het eten.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "513c4682-3d4a-43e1-8d23-e18ebc055814"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sofia is sometimes mistaken.",
        "note": "zich belongs to zich vergissen."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Sofia vergist zich soms.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "f25c51ed-a606-43cd-bad9-41196b154d9d"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "warning",
        "icon": "triangle-alert"
      },
      "content": "With ik, use me: Ik voel me. Do not say: Ik voel zich.",
      "id": "69e8568e-41e4-421b-bdd3-524ed3955f16"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "hint",
        "icon": "lightbulb"
      },
      "content": "Memorize the verb and its pronoun as one unit: zich voelen, zich wassen, zich aankleden, zich vergissen.",
      "id": "1eb85091-77d6-467b-8bb3-4e86221a53a3"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "zich wassen",
              "meaning": "to wash oneself",
              "forms": "wast zich · waste zich · zich gewassen",
              "example": "Ik was me thuis.",
              "id": "18af5891-c9f9-4ff6-aa89-568094d7e428"
            },
            {
              "term": "zich aankleden",
              "meaning": "to get dressed",
              "forms": "kleedt zich aan · kleedde zich aan · zich aangekleed",
              "example": "Sofia wil zich aankleden.",
              "id": "9d37c9a1-3714-4836-995f-1b070fea41fd"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "e335f7eb-4e87-42a5-85b9-c0ef52626a75"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "With an infinitive",
      "id": "8a1a7510-90d9-4767-8132-206da6594437"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "When the reflexive verb is an infinitive, keep its pronoun with it: Ik wil me wassen. In a short purpose phrase, use om me aan te kleden. These are examples, not a full catalogue of reflexive grammar.",
      "id": "7324e3de-9acb-4359-ad8b-9aec950b2a57"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "I want to wash myself.",
        "note": "The pronoun stays with the infinitive wassen."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Ik wil me wassen.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "86675723-ceba-4ea4-8444-d1d4f1b7904f"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sofia wants to get dressed.",
        "note": "The pronoun stays with aankleden."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Sofia wil zich aankleden.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "01270d98-83d9-4cf3-b057-c0882f567523"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "props": {
        "translation": "Piotr is not mistaken.",
        "note": "The negation follows the reflexive pronoun."
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Piotr vergist zich niet.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        }
      ],
      "id": "2323544d-12b9-4198-9971-4c8005471949"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "grammar",
        "icon": "message-circle-warning"
      },
      "content": "Ik voel me niet lekker describes how someone feels. Ik ben ziek says “I am ill”; do not use the reflexive form with ziek.",
      "id": "55735a01-649b-4fce-a28a-081dcca6915b"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Formal requests at a service desk",
      "id": "152bd9e6-4b8b-43c4-ac34-8ca6e2174946"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Use u with a doctor’s office or a municipal service worker in these models. Kunt u…? asks politely; Wilt u…? asks what the other person would like to do. Zou u … kunnen? is a careful request.",
      "id": "c5e751fc-6793-41d2-bf28-e0d52cef2562"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "important",
        "icon": "star"
      },
      "content": "Keep u consistent: Kunt u …? / Wilt u …? / Zou u … kunnen? Close with alstublieft and dank u wel.",
      "id": "f0c67a52-0702-47ee-85c4-02dcaeb14f44"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "Greet the staff member: Goedemiddag.",
      "id": "72516a4f-dcd1-4581-a5de-2d44bc391bae"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "Say what you need: Ik wil graag een afspraak maken.",
      "id": "fdd05956-d817-48b1-b001-46238ec884f8"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "Ask one clear question: Kunt u mij helpen?",
      "id": "a6c859cc-a819-4fcd-a233-c82bd1e4e49c"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "If needed, ask for repetition: Zou u dat kunnen herhalen, alstublieft?",
      "id": "c774278b-0e1b-4b10-aded-11c91525a03f"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "Useful service words",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "de afspraak — appointment",
          "id": "d67f443c-d411-4f54-b667-73e49a344f02"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "het formulier — form",
          "id": "052cbbc1-dd12-43ac-ac13-17c9fa641421"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "de balie — service counter",
          "id": "e49ff0f1-2863-474f-a9d2-daa4f1961e5a"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "a copy of the form",
          "id": "ca5bfccb-a112-40fb-a1c6-7c2ad4591272"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "a blank copy",
          "id": "0151ead4-f7ff-4ddb-aeb5-240c232da0b7"
        }
      ],
      "id": "c282c3d6-1f03-431d-9d97-b448def0bce5"
    },
    {
